# Mcore
(actual format JSON-based or sexp)

~ Begin Figure { #fig-mcore-syntax-complete; caption: "Syntax of MCore"; tex-float-placement: "h" }
~ Begin Figblock { caption: "Program Syntax"; .small }

|:~~{.labelcol}~~~~~~~~~~|~~{.vcol}~|~~~~~~~~|~~{.defcol}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~{.desccol}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|
| Terms                  | $term$   | $::=$  | $x : T$                                                 | (typed) variables        |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $fn (\many{x : T}). term$                               | abstraction              |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $term term$                                             | application              |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $\many{term}; term$                                     | sequencing               |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $let \many{defi} in term$                               |                          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $letrec \many{defi} in term$                            |                          |
|                        | *control:*                                                              ||                          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $fresh label$      | generating labels |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $reset L at x : T with (\many{x : T}) term in term$      | reset/prompt |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $let x:T = shift L n in term$      | shift |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $let x:T = control L n in term$      | control |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $resume term (\many{term})$      | resume (with args) |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $resumed term in term$      | resume (with program that returns) |
|                        | *data, codata:*                                                            ||                          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $construct C (\many{term})$                             | data type construction   |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $project {term} C f$                                    | data type projection   |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $match {term} \{\many{ C(\many{x}): term}\}$            | data type match       |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $new I \{\many{M(\many{x : T}) => term}\}$      | codata/object construction|
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $invoke term I.M (\many{term})$      | method invokation |
|                        | *references:*                                                              ||                          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $letref x : T = term at term in term$      | allocation in region |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $load term$      | load from reference |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $store term term$      | store in reference |
|                        | ... *primitives, literals, if0, switch*                                                              ||                          |
| Definitions            | $defi$   | $::=$  | $x : T = term$
| Types                  | $T$      |        |                                                         |                          |

~ End Figblock
~ End Figure

# Asm
(actual format similar or JSON-based)

~ Begin Figure { #fig-asm-syntax-complete; caption: "Syntax of ASM"; tex-float-placement: "h" }
~ Begin Figblock { caption: "Program Syntax"; .small }

|:~~{.labelcol}~~~~~~~~~~|~~{.vcol}~|~~~~~~~~|~~{.defcol}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~{.desccol}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|
| Instructions           | $stmt$   | $::=$  | $let \many{x <- y}$                                     | register movement        |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $let const x <- n$                                      | constant integers        |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $\many{y} <- primitive N (\many{x})$                    | primitive operations/"FFI" |
|                        |          | *if0, switch, other constants ...*                              ||                          |
|                        | *control:*                                                                |||                          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $push l(\many{x})$                                      | pushing a frame          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $return (\many{x})$                                     |                          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $jump l(\many{x})$                                      |                          |
|                        |                                                                           |||                          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $y <- shift x_{n} x_{p}$                                | shift (w. label + offset) |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $y <- control x_{n} x_{p}$                              | control (ditto)          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $y, y_{r} <- new stack x_{p} l (\many{x})$              | (meta)stack creation (with region and prompt)     |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $push stack x$                                          | pushing a stack          |
|                        | *data, codata:*                                                           |||                          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $y <- construct C (\many{x})$                           | data type construction   |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $y <- project x C f$                                    | data type projection     |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $match x \{\many{C(\many{y}): l(\many{x})}\}$           | data type match          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $y <- new I \{\many{M: l}\} (\many{x})$                 | codata/object creation   |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $invoke x M (\many{x})$                                 | method invokation        |
|                        | *references:*                                                             |||                          |
|                        |          | *(new stack, see above)*                                        ||                          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $y <- allocate x_{r} (x)$                               | allocation in region     |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $y <- load x$                                           | load from reference      |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $store x x$                                             | store in reference       |
~ End Figblock
~ End Figure

# RPyeffect
(actual format JSON-based)

Very similar to ASM. Most notable differences: Registers are indices, some restrictions on arguments for jumps etc, register movement in explicit small instructions.

~ Begin Figure { #fig-jit-syntax-complete; caption: "Syntax of the bytecode format &BC;."; tex-float-placement: "h" }

~ Begin Small

~ Begin Figblock { caption: "Program Syntax"; .small }

|:~~{.labelcol}~~~~~~~~~~|~~{.vcol}~|~~~~~~~~|~~{.defcol}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|~~{.desccol}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~|
| Program                | $program$| $::=$  | $\many{B_i}$                                            | programs                 |
| Blocks                 | $B$      | $::=$  | $\{ label(\many{x_i}): stmt \}$                    | basic blocks             |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $label$                                                 | block labels             |
| Statements             | $stmt$   | $::=$  | $x <- v; stmt$                                          | literals / constants     |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $\many{x_i} <- primitive f(\many{x_j}); stmt$           | primitive calls          |
| $\quad$_jumps_ |||||
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $jump B$                                                | jump                     |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $if x_1 then B(\many{x_i}) else stmt$                   | conditional jump         |
| $\quad$_stack management_ |||||
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $push B (\many{x_i}); stmt$                             | push a frame             |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $return (\many{x_i})$                                   | return                   |
| $\quad$_metastack management_ |||||
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $x_1 <- shift x_2; stmt$                                | capturing stacks         |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $x <- new stack B(\many{x_i}); stmt$                    | creating new stacks      |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $push stack x; stmt$                                    | pushing a stack          |
| $\quad$_objects_ |||||
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $x <- new V(\many{x_j}); stmt$                          | object creation          |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $x.m(\many{x_i})$                                       | method invocation        |
| $\quad$_data_ |||||
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $x <- tag(\many{x_i}); stmt$                            | data construction        |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $x match \{\many{tag(\many{x_i}) => B}\}$               | matching                 |
| $\quad$_register management_ |||||
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $x_1 <- x_2; stmt$                                      | copying                  |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $x_1 \leftrightarrow{} x_2; stmt$                         | swapping                 |
|                        |          | $\pip$ | $drop x; stmt$                                          | dropping                 |
| VTables                | $V$      | $::=$  | $\{\many{m_i \mapsto B_i}\}$                            | virtual table            |
| Labels and tags        | $label$, $tag$, $m$ |
| Variables              | $x$ |

~ End Figblock

~ End Small
~ End Figure

